You need to fix two major bugs in `/sessions/stoic-relaxed-carson/mnt/outputs/interactive-mockup.html`:

## BUG 1: Card selection (yellow border) doesn't work
The `selectCard` function uses `data-section` to find sibling cards, but cards DON'T have a `data-section` attribute. They only have `data-var` and `data-val`.

FIX: Replace the selectCard function to use `.closest('.dc-section')` to find the parent section, then deselect all sibling cards within it:
```javascript
function selectCard(c) {
  var section = c.closest('.dc-section');
  if (section) {
    section.querySelectorAll('.dc-card').forEach(function(x) { x.classList.remove('selected'); });
  }
  c.classList.add('selected');
  var v = c.getAttribute('data-var');
  var val = c.getAttribute('data-val');
  if (v && val && v !== 'visual-only') {
    updateRootVar('--' + v, val);
  }
}
```

## BUG 2: Other tabs (Landing, Upload, About You, Target Banks, Results) are EMPTY
The tab buttons exist but the corresponding `<div id="tab-landing">`, `<div id="tab-upload">` etc. content divs are missing from the HTML.

FIX: Add content divs for each tab AFTER the `tab-compare` closing div and BEFORE the control panel. Each tab should contain a realistic mockup of that page from the original site (https://ib-resume-os-yd67.vercel.app/) styled with CSS custom properties so they react to design changes.

Here's what each tab should contain (use CSS custom properties like var(--heading-font), var(--body-font), var(--accent-gold), var(--bg-card), var(--border-radius), etc.):

### tab-landing:
- Top nav bar: "IB Resume BA" logo (left), "Export PDF" and "Re-upload" buttons (right)
- Scrolling bank ticker bar: "GOLDMAN SACHS  ·  MORGAN STANLEY  ·  JP MORGAN  ·  BARCLAYS  ·  EVERCORE  ·  LAZARD  ·  MOELIS  ·  PJT PARTNERS"
- Hero section: "- PRIVATE ACCESS ONLY -" label, "Built for IB recruiting." heading (using var(--heading-font)), "Unfiltered." in gold italic (using var(--accent-font) + var(--accent-gold))
- Subtitle: "See your resume the way IB recruiters see it..."
- Stats: "18+ BANK PROFILES", "14+ FORMAT CHECKS", "100 POINT SCORE"
- Access code form card: "Enter your access code" with input fields and "Continue →" button

### tab-upload:
- Heading: "Upload your resume"
- Drag-and-drop upload area with dashed border
- "PDF only, max 2 pages" note
- Progress indicator (step 1 of 3)

### tab-about:
- Heading: "Tell us about yourself"
- Form fields: School (dropdown), Year (dropdown), Target role
- Progress indicator (step 2 of 3)

### tab-banks:
- Heading: "Select your target banks"
- Grid of bank cards with logos/names: Goldman Sachs, Morgan Stanley, JP Morgan, etc.
- "Continue" button

### tab-results:
- Score circle: "95 / 100" with green ring
- "INTERVIEW-READY" badge
- "Your resume is highly competitive for top IB roles." heading
- Category scores: FORMAT 15/15, EDUCATION 15/15, EXPERIENCE 30/30, BULLETS 20/25, POSITIONING 15/15
- Progress bars for each
- CRITICAL FIXES section with issue cards (left-border colored cards)
- Before → After rewrite section
- BANK FIT ANALYSIS sidebar: Evercore "Strong", Goldman Sachs "Moderate"
- IB FORMAT CHECKLIST with pass/fail items

IMPORTANT STYLE RULES to match the original:
- Background: var(--bg-body) = #0A0A0A
- Card backgrounds: var(--bg-card) = #141312
- Card borders: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08)
- Border radius: var(--border-radius)
- Heading font: var(--heading-font)
- Body font: var(--body-font)
- Gold accent: var(--accent-gold) for buttons, accents
- Green: var(--color-green) for scores, pass indicators
- Red: var(--color-red) for critical issues
- Orange: var(--color-orange) for warnings
- Text: var(--text-primary) and var(--text-secondary)

## APPROACH:
The file is minified (single line, ~88KB). Use Python to:
1. Read the file
2. Find and fix the selectCard function
3. Find where to insert the tab content divs (after tab-compare's closing div)
4. Insert the 5 tab content divs
5. Write back

Also update the saveTheme function to export a proper manifest.json instead of just CSS:
```javascript
function saveTheme() {
  var manifest = {
    generatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
    cssVariables: {},
    selections: {}
  };
  // Collect CSS variables
  var r = document.documentElement.style;
  for (var i = 0; i < r.length; i++) {
    var v = r[i];
    if (v.startsWith('--')) {
      manifest.cssVariables[v] = r.getPropertyValue(v).trim();
    }
  }
  // Collect selected cards
  document.querySelectorAll('.dc-card.selected').forEach(function(card) {
    var section = card.closest('.dc-section');
    var title = section ? section.querySelector('.dc-section-title').textContent : 'unknown';
    var label = card.querySelector('.dc-label span').textContent;
    manifest.selections[title] = label;
  });
  // Download manifest
  var a = document.createElement('a');
  a.href = 'data:application/json;charset=utf-8,' + encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(manifest, null, 2));
  a.download = 'design-manifest.json';
  a.click();
}
```

Run the Python script after writing. Verify:
- All 5 tab IDs found in output
- selectCard function uses closest('.dc-section')
- saveTheme generates manifest.json
- File size is reasonable (should be ~120-150KB with all tab content)

